{"id":"polychrome","title":"Polychrome","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Polychrome","rev":239855,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Polychrome"]}," is a graphic design aesthetic that originated in the early 2010s. It was mostly used by electronic pop artists and advisements for commercial brands, film, etc. The style is named after the album of the same title by electric pop duo Koan Sound, which features the aesthetic in its cover art. It is characterized by heavy use of abstract and blended colorful patterns, usually generated through natural means."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The visual style of Polychrome is characterized by colors bursting/mixing together, usually over simple white/black backgrounds. This includes ink/liquid spills, powder explosions, smoke, paint smears and splatters, oil slicks, blended watercolors, plastic shimmers. etc. The palette uses a wide variety of color gradients, mostly blue, red, orange, yellow and turquoise."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Brands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Nintendo (DS and 3DS)"]},{"c":["Playstation"]},{"c":["Xbox"]},{"c":["Windows"]},{"c":["Vaio"]},{"c":["Lenovo"]},{"c":["Apple (iPod)"]},{"c":["Nike"]},{"c":["Adidas"]},{"c":["Mio"]},{"c":["Costco"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4c/Original_67faab2f85a7202ce900528073d4e356.png/revision/latest?cb=20260209162919","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/29/Original_cd2f3e7d3fe232940e42d6416c8045f8.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260209163659","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a1/Original_802a396ca95943fff8083ee0bb284b0e.png/revision/latest?cb=20260209163722","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Apple \"Color Burst 3\" Wallpaper"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/im